WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Start with the builder. The header gives you documentation, theme, and release choices.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Choose Custom to combine runtime and hardware paths, or start with a vendor path. [Click Custom]

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.000
The configuration page starts with target architectures and the Kubernetes distribution. [Custom]

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Choose the architecture of your target nodes. [Click AMD64]

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Select the Kubernetes distribution used by your cluster. [Click kubeadm]

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Choose a runtime. The highlighted option is QEMU. [Click QEMU]

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Select the runtime you want to install. KRAB checks the architecture coverage as you choose. [AMD64 · kubeadm · QEMU]

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Review the version-pinned Helm command and generated values before deploying. [Review the output]

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Export the same configuration to continue in your terminal. [Click Continue in TUI / CLI]

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Download values for Helm, or export krab.json to keep working in the TUI and CLI. [Continue in TUI / CLI]
